.TH SLEEP 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
sleep \- wait for a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleep
.I seconds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sleep
waits
.I seconds
seconds, then exits. The number may have a fraction
.RB ( "sleep 0.5" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after the wait; 1, with a usage message, when
.I seconds
is missing or isn't a number.
.SH NOTES
Only one argument is read; there are no unit suffixes
.RB ( s ,
.BR m ,
.BR h ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR time (1)
